"""
Vector periodic clock: plants a common `dt` periodic clock on `n` nodes.

Vector analogue of `DiscreteComponents.PeriodicClock`, templated like
`MatrixGain` (structural channel count, array port via comprehension). Each
channel carries an independent `PeriodicClock(dt)`; because all channels share
the same period, they unify to a single clock partition wherever they are
gathered downstream (e.g. all `n` outputs connected to the input vector of one
clocked block such as `DiscreteStateSpace`, whose shared block clock ties the
channels together).

A single fanned clock cannot be used: connecting one `PeriodicClock.y` to `n`
boundary ports would merge all `n` ports into one connection set, which then
merges every channel at the point of use (the illegal "two inner output
connectors in the same set" case). Independent per-channel clocks keep the
`n` connection sets separate; the block clock at the point of use performs the
unification.

Connectors:
- `y :: RealInput[n]` — clock-carrying ports (mirrors `PeriodicClock.y`, which is
  itself a `RealInput`: connect a clocked node here to force it onto the clock).

Parameters:
- `n`  — number of channels.
- `dt` — clock period (same units as `time`).
"""
component VectorClock
  "Number of channels."
  structural parameter n::Integer = 1
  "Clock period."
  structural parameter dt::Real
  "Clock-carrying ports (one per channel)."
  y = [RealInput() for i in 1:n] {^y}
  "Per-channel periodic clocks, all at the same period `dt`."
  c = [DiscreteComponents.PeriodicClock(dt = dt) for i in 1:n]
relations
  for i in 1:n
    connect(c[i].y, y[i])
  end
metadata {
  "Dyad": {"icons": {"default": "dyad://F16ModelWorkshop/vector_clock.svg"}},
  "_links": {
    "y": {
      "Dyad": {
        "placement": {
          "diagram": {"iconName": "default", "x1": 0, "y1": 450, "x2": 100, "y2": 550, "rot": 0}
        },
        "tags": []
      }
    }
  }
}
end
